      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most significant weakness in the UBI argument is the massive, unsustainable cost, which critics rightly point out will require crippling tax hikes or massive national debt. Furthermore, the idea that people will use guaranteed income to pursue meaningful work is a fallacy; many will simply choose not to work, leading to labor shortages and economic stagnation. A strong rebuttal is to demand concrete, fiscally responsible funding mechanisms rather than relying on vague promises of economic growth.",
